					<description><![CDATA[<p>Highland Europe Closes €1.1 Billion Growth Fund Highland Europe raises $1.25bn fund Highland Europe has raised a total of $1.25 billion in its latest fundraising round to strengthen its standing</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/highland-europe-raises-1-25-billion/" data-wpel-link="internal">Highland Europe Raises $1.25 Billion To Back Growth-Stage Tech Companies</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Highland Europe Closes €1.1 Billion Growth Fund</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Highland Europe raises $1.25bn fund Highland Europe has raised a total of $1.25 billion in its latest fundraising round to strengthen its standing as a go-to growth-stage European tech investor globally. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Fund VI caps off a remarkable run with the company having returned over $1bn to its limited partners through multiple major exits of its portfolio companies within a year. Highland Europe has now closed six funds raising in the region of €3.75bn since its founding in 2012.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The investment will pursue its strategy of investing in technology businesses with product-market fit. Investors include existing LP&#8217;s and the company said the fund will invest across enterprise software, FinTech, healthcare, AI and consumer technology companies.</span></p>
<h2><b>Major Portfolio Exits Fuel Investor Confidence</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Highland Europe&#8217;s latest fundraising comes after a strong year of portfolio realisations. Among its most notable exits was the approximately $3 billion sale of digital employee experience platform Nexthink. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The firm&#8217;s portfolio company Bending Spoons also reached an estimated market capitalisation of more than $18 billion following its Nasdaq listing, highlighting the increasing global profile of European technology companies.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Highland Europe has backed over 80 businesses and has completed around 30 exits since it started. Portfolio companies generate more than $6 billion in annual revenues and employ in excess of 15,000 people across the globe.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Partner Sam Brooks stated, “Ongoing commitments from our limited partners allow us to continue supporting promising European founders in the midst of transformational developments in the use of AI across global economic industries.”</span></p>
<h2><b>Fund VI Targets AI And Global Expansion<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203859" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203859" class="size-full wp-image-203859" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/a-futuristic-poster-depicts-a-sprawling-_OkUekmrTVg6_68sWGOztXw_tvC60s3xSyqFpqULB0TvlQ.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing venture capital funding flowing into AI-driven global technology companies." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203859" class="wp-caption-text">Highland Europe backs AI-driven companies scaling across industries and global markets. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Highland Europe specialises in investing after companies have established stable revenues and customer demand, providing capital that helps businesses expand internationally, strengthen leadership teams, and accelerate product innovation.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Recent investments illustrate this strategy. The firm recently led funding rounds for legal AI platform Wordsmith and enterprise AI workflow company Unframe. It also participated in a major financing round for </span><a href="https://www.britannica.com/science/precision-measurement" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">precision</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> agriculture technology company Ecorobotix.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Highland believes artificial intelligence will continue creating significant opportunities across enterprise software and industry-specific technology. The firm also intends to back companies using AI to transform established sectors such as healthcare, financial services, and industrial operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This approach has also supported previous investments in companies including n8n, Nabla, 9fin, Nothing, Camunda, and Zwift, all of which operate in rapidly growing technology markets. Consumer nutrition brand Huel also agreed to an acquisition by Danone. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/groundcover-raises-100-million/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">groundcover Raises $100 Million To Expand AI-Era Observability Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Leadership Promotions Support Long-Term Strategy</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Alongside the new fund, Highland Europe promoted Helena Richardson and Jacob Bernstein to partner positions. Richardson joined the firm in 2016 and has worked closely with consumer and fintech businesses, including Huel, Modulr, ME+EM, and Ffern.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Bernstein, who joined in 2017, focuses primarily on enterprise technology investments, including Unframe, Zero Networks, Oritain, and Descartes Underwriting. Their promotions expand Highland&#8217;s senior leadership while maintaining its equal partnership structure.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">With fresh capital available through Fund VI, Highland Europe plans to continue supporting growth-stage technology companies as they scale internationally and compete in increasingly AI-driven markets. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
