					<description><![CDATA[<p>Just four months after its $35 million Series A round, Onyx raises in a $113 million Series B round to bring its valuation to $640. The investment round was led</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/onyx-security-raises-113-million-series-b-ai-agent-governance/" data-wpel-link="internal">Onyx Security Raises $113 Million Series B To Scale Next-Gen AI Agent Governance Models</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Just four months after its $35 million </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/onyx-security-raises-40m-to-expand-cybersecurity-platform/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Series A round</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">, Onyx raises in a $113 million Series B round to bring its valuation to $640. The investment round was led by Bessemer Venture Partners. Additional backing came from Cyberstarts, TCV, Conviction, FirstMark, Vintage, QuantumLight, and G Squared.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Organizations are adopting powerful autonomous agents for complex internal workflows. However, these tools often operate without clear boundary lines or safety guardrails. The latest funding will help Onyx scale its services to solve that exact problem for enterprises.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Onyx Security is Taming Autonomous AI in the Enterprise</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203855" style="width: 1034px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203855" class="size-large wp-image-203855" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Onyx-1024x618.jpeg" alt="A hero style image showing Security Raises $113M and all the partners led by Bessemer Venture Partners and joined by Cyberstarts, TCV, Conviction, FirstMark, Vintage, QuantumLight, and G Squared" width="1024" height="618" /><p id="caption-attachment-203855" class="wp-caption-text">Onyx Security Raises $113M</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Artificial intelligence is moving beyond basic chatbots to fully autonomous agents. Now employees have direct access to sensitive data and core operational tasks, as well as critical systems, by granting AI agents direct access to these systems. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">While these agents boost productivity, they present a massive governance challenge. Autonomous actors perform complex actions without standard human accountability or oversight. In 2025, AI agents handled less than one percent of digital tasks in most organizations. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">That figure is set to explode as companies adopt next-generation reasoning models like Mythos and Fable. As of now, most of the enterprise actions are carried out by autonomous actors, </span><a href="https://www.onyx.security/blog/onyx-113m-series-b-keeping-humans-in-control-as-ai-becomes-smarter" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">pointed out</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> by Onyx co-founder and CEO Maxim Bar Kogan. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">If there’s no governance, businesses can suffer data breaches, unapproved code releases, and unexpected system issues. Onyx provides teams with the visibility they need to avoid those problems from happening.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/tech-giants-commit-265-million-on-electricians-data-centers/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Tech Giants Commit $265M To Data Center Electricians</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">How Onyx’s Control Plane Operates</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Onyx acts as a dedicated control layer for artificial intelligence. The startup uses proprietary security models to track each step of an AI agent’s reasoning process. If an agent attempts an unauthorized, unexpected, or malicious step, the system intervenes instantly. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This runtime intervention allows security and IT teams to monitor autonomous behavior without blocking productivity. The platform works seamlessly across both custom internal tools and third-party commercial agents. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Organizations can enforce internal compliance rules, set strict operational parameters, and block risky behavior in real time. Uros Solar, Head of Security Engineering at Revolut, highlighted how Onyx helps evaluate and stop threats during execution. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">That capability gives security leaders the confidence to roll out AI tools across critical software development and operational environments.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/freehand-raises-75-million-ai-agents-supply-chain/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Freehand Raises $75M for AI Agents in Supply Chains</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Rapid Revenue Growth and Global Expansion</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Demand for AI governance has pushed Onyx into rapid growth mode. The company quadrupled its revenue in just four months after leaving stealth mode. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">A major milestone arrived in June, when Anthropic partnered with Onyx to secure enterprise deployments of its models. Dozens of other leading AI developers have integrated their systems into the Onyx platform as well.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Onyx is used by Fortune 500 companies in banking, technology, insurance, and energy today for AI security. Trust and accountability are essential for the successful adoption of AI, and Bessemer Venture Partners saw this early on.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">With $113 in new capital, Onyx plans to advance its proprietary machine learning models. The startup will also expand its sales and engineering operations across North America and international markets.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/qureight-raises-20m-series-b-ai-lung-heart-clinical-trials/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Qureight Raises $20M for AI-powered Lung and Heart Clinical Trials</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/onyx-security-raises-113-million-series-b-ai-agent-governance/" data-wpel-link="internal">Onyx Security Raises $113 Million Series B To Scale Next-Gen AI Agent Governance Models</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
