										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>groundcover Raises $100 Million To Scale AI Observability</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">groundcover has raised $100 million. The new funding round was co-led by new investors One Peak and Morgan Stanley Expansion Capital. Zeev Ventures, Angular Ventures, Heavybit, and Jibe also took part in the funding.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding rounds bring the total the Tel Aviv, Israel-based company has raised to $160 million. groundcover announced it would use the funding for its worldwide rollout, deepen collaboration agreements with top cloud suppliers, accelerate and speed up product innovation. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">It serves clients in more than 250 enterprises &#8211; many of themFortune 5 companies alongside fast-starting startups- and tripled its </span><a href="https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/revenue.asp" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">revenue</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> while doubling its worldwide employees to 130 workers throughout the world during the last year.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI Growth Drives Demand For Modern Observability</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Given the growing amount of workloads deployed that utilize AI or run as autonomous systems, engineering teams need increased insight into the infrastructure, applications and the AI workloads within them, without compromising on the cost or data security/privacy.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">groundcover brings to combine adaptive eBPF sensors with an off-the-shelf OpenTelemetry support to produce complete telemetry across infrastructure, applications and AI workloads, with no data sampling. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">&#8220;We are entering the era of AI, and that requires a new model of observability, different from the one that we have today,&#8221; said CEO Shahar Azulay, founder of groundcover. We leverage eBPF and our BYOC infrastructure to give our customers a platform that has the ability to serve engineers andAutonomous AI agents that run in production environments.</span></p>
<h2><b>Platform Supports Autonomous Operations<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203844" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203844" class="size-full wp-image-203844" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/remove_4-v-vQJyXK-Ky53LAEUhXQ_aKr_5m4VRBGKbTfw0ahd-A_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI observability systems with full data visibility and autonomous monitoring agents." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203844" class="wp-caption-text">groundcover enables full-data observability and autonomous issue resolution for AI-native cloud environments. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Unlike traditional observability platforms that reduce or sample telemetry data to manage costs, groundcover captures full-fidelity operational data while keeping it within customers&#8217; own cloud environments. This approach enables organisations to maintain privacy, reduce operational overhead, and improve AI-driven decision-making.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company&#8217;s Agent Mode further extends these capabilities by helping engineering teams automatically identify, troubleshoot, and remediate production issues. By providing complete operational visibility, groundcover aims to create the data foundation required for autonomous software operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">One Peak said the company has developed an observability platform specifically designed for AI-native environments. The investment firm believes groundcover&#8217;s architecture positions it to define the next generation of observability infrastructure as enterprises increasingly rely on AI-powered applications.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform has gained traction across organisations seeking greater control over operational data while reducing dependence on legacy monitoring solutions that struggle with rapidly growing telemetry volumes.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/investifi-raises-20-million/" data-wpel-link="internal">InvestiFi Raises $20 Million To Expand Digital Investing For Credit Unions</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Funding To Accelerate Global Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">groundcover plans to use the new funding to strengthen its commercial operations, particularly across North America, where it continues to win customers from established observability providers. The company also intends to expand into additional international markets while deepening its co-sell programmes with leading cloud providers.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Investment will also support the continued expansion of the product roadmap, including new AI-powered capabilities and additional observability use cases. The company aims to build a platform that enables engineers and autonomous AI agents to work together more effectively while maintaining full control over operational data.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As enterprises continue adopting AI across critical business systems, observability is becoming an increasingly important layer of cloud infrastructure. groundcover is positioning itself to capitalise on this shift by delivering scalable monitoring, privacy-first architecture, and AI-enabled automation for modern software environments.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
